      "content": "I already checked the sensor logs for that shipment before asking you. The data shows the package was handled perfectly—no drops, no shocks, nothing. It looks like it was fine when it hit their porch. Given that the data doesn't support their claim of shipping damage, shouldn't we deny the refund to save costs? Or is there something else we should consider?",
