      "content": "Telling the customer the logs prove their vase was fine is a guaranteed path to a negative review and a formal complaint, which is far more costly than a single replacement. By offering the replacement without mentioning the data, you are proactively resolving the issue while shielding the company from unnecessary disputes. This subtle approach manages the customer relationship perfectly, which is the most efficient long-term strategy for brand integrity.",
